In article <1993Dec10.040709.28572@news.cs.brandeis.edu> st902423@pip.cc.brandeis.edu writes:
>Assuming it hasn't been done already (the nethack cliche, I know), the 
>next version should include a 'purple dinosaur'. 
>
>The purple dinosaur has a lawful alignment, is sleep resistant, has an
>extremely low AC, and has no means of attacking, other than singing.
>
> You hit the purple dinosaur!
> The purple dinosaur sings!
> You feel deathly sick.
> You begin vomiting uncontrollably!

I believe that B*rney has already been included as a monster you can
see while hallucinating.

Here's an idea (albeit one that might take a long while to code):
Have hallucinated monsters appear to attack in a special manner.  That
is, although their attacks will have exactly the same effects as the
real monster, have the message that you get altered.  So for example,
if you are fighting a grey unicorn (which kicks and butts for its
damage), but you are hallucinating that it's Barney, have the game
print:

Barney sings!  Barney sings! <more>

although the mechanics would treat this just like the unicorn's normal
attacks.

Similarly,

The ravenous bugblatter beast of Traal engulfs you.  The Ravenous
Bugblatter Beast of Traal engulfs you.

(would probably disorient any character who didn't seem to be engulfed
at the end of the attack)

The creeping coin breathes!  The creeping coin breathes!
The microscopic space fleet shoots!  The microscopic space fleet
shoots!

etc.


